integ5 0087 = patches/glue5/0072-tests-glm-shared-check-e4m3-pages.patch (overnight 2026-10-31), renumbered for the integrated stack on 3f94715d.

tests: glm-shared-check on E4M3 KV pages (TF_GLM_CHECK_KV8=1 TF_KV_PAGES=on, glm-pair-check's switches); v2

Every stream and twin on pages of one pool (poisoned: a row read before its write turns the reply to NaN), so the
check compares shared windows, whose latent attention takes the segment-batched launches on E4M3 pages (0070),
against their lone twins byte for byte: logits, tokens, drafts and states. Without the switches it runs as before.
v2: on pages a state's arena ends in its page table, whose ids differ between a stream and its twin (each slot
leases its own pages), so the arena is compared up to the table, and then every page of the stream's against its
twin's page at the same table index (the KV rows: codes and scales or bf16, pooled keys, the MTP head's part; the
tails poisoned alike). v1 compared the whole arena: on pages it failed on the table's first id and never compared
the pages.

